    643  f9a1							; ==============================================================================
    644  f9a1							; HcrClock — hcrunch animation clock (fixed full=10 since 2026-10-19).
    645  f9a1							;   In:  X = full extent (cells, ≥1); reads EnemyRamP (StartFrame-pinned)
    646  f9a1							;   Out: A = covered (1..full) — never 0 (always-solid stub)
    647  f9a1							;   Clobbers A (X/Y preserved — unlike CrunchClock). No latch: the kill
    648  f9a1							;   repeats on contact (DropArm respawns at the room top, so no loop).
    649  f9a1							; s = EnemyRamP>>4 (0..15, one 256f period = 16 buckets of 16f):
    650  f9a1							;   s 0-3   dwell at home  (eff 0)	  -> n=1, 64f stub
    651  f9a1							;   s 4-12  grow to center  (eff s-3)	  -> n 2..full (1..9 cells of
    652  f9a1							;	    8px — full=w>>1; w=20 record = center of the screen)
    653  f9a1							;   s 13-15 fast retract    (eff 3*(15-s) = 6,3,0) — wipe home in 3
    654  f9a1							;	    steps (the old instant far-end turn, stretched to center)
    655  f9a1							; covered = 1 + min(eff, full-1). CrunchClock (sc>>2 triangle, ~4f/step)
    656  f9a1							; stays for its VCR mirrors + verify_build token gate — only the two
    657  f9a1							; hcrunch call sites moved here (16f/step, grow-to-center ruling
    658  f9a1							; 2026-10-16). Both callers pass full=10 (PhHcrEntry stages it, HOV
    659  f9a1							; tests it); the latch freeze was removed with the 2026-10-19 contract.
    660  f9a1							; ==============================================================================
